Package: powerscope
Title: Power, Sample Size, and Type S/M Errors for Genomics Study Designs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Abdulhadi", "Kobiowu", , "somatohadidas@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes statistical power, required sample size, minimum
    detectable effect, sign error rate (Type S) and exaggeration ratio
    (Type M) for two-group comparisons of means and proportions,
    negative binomial RNA-seq differential expression, pooled-sequencing
    allele-frequency differences, case-control allelic association and
    quantitative-trait association. Every design is reduced to an effect
    and its standard error and passed through one shared engine
    following Gelman and Carlin (2014) <doi:10.1177/1745691614551642>.
    Per-test significance levels that control the false discovery rate
    across many tests follow Jung (2005) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bti456>.
